2026-11-24  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	The proof of concept works: u2netp.onnx runs from JavaScript.

	* tests/u2netp-poc.js:
	New, first version from the nemotron harness session. Loads
	u2netp.onnx, builds the blob with qjs-opencv exactly as
	opencv-imgproc.js runSalient does, runs it through ort and through
	OpenCV dnn, compares the raw outputs (max abs difference 7.6e-5,
	limit 1e-3), writes the matte to .tmp/u2netp-matte.png and runs 25
	rounds that must give identical results. Fixed after review: the
	model path ignored its argument when WB_MODELS_DIR was set (a ??
	and ?: precedence bug), and the OpenCV time included loading the
	network, now shown separately.

	* TODO.md:
	Rewritten as a status page: PoC reached, the install rpath of the
	installed ort.so first, the later list after it.

2026-11-24  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	The installed ort.so can find ONNX Runtime.

	* CMakeLists.txt:
	New option INSTALL_ORT_LIBRARY, on by default when ONNX Runtime comes
	from third_party/ or ORT_PREFIX. Install rules put
	libonnxruntime.so.1 (the real file, not the symlink) and
	libonnxruntime_providers_shared.so into the C module directory, which
	is already in the RUNPATH of ort.so. A system copy of ONNX Runtime
	needs nothing. Checked with a DESTDIR install: the loader resolves
	libonnxruntime.so.1 there, and tests/u2netp-poc.js passes from that
	tree (max abs difference 7.6e-5).

	* CLAUDE.md (Build & run), TODO.md:
	Notes updated, the install rpath item is done.
